│ patch_name               │ reduce_params_add_parametrized_entanglement                                               │
│ patch_description        │ This edit aims to improve the combined score by:                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Reducing parameter count through strategic parameter sharing on pre/post RZ rotations  │
│                          │ (currently 18 unique params for 18 gates)                                                 │
│                          │ 2. Replacing some fixed CZ gates with parametrized CRZ gates to enable learned            │
│                          │ entanglement patterns                                                                     │
│                          │ 3. Adding parametrized three-qubit ZZZ gates for richer interactions                      │
│                          │ 4. This should reduce overfitting (narrower train-test gap), improve test accuracy, and   │
│                          │ increase parameter efficiency                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The trade-off is slightly more gates, but with better information encoding through        │
│                          │ parametrized two-qubit and three-qubit interactions rather than just single-qubit         │
│                          │ rotations and fixed gates.                                                                │
