│ patch_description        │ This edit enhances the ansatz by:                                                         │
│                          │ 1. Adding RX gates alongside RY gates for better single-qubit expressivity (rotation      │
│                          │ around different axis)                                                                    │
│                          │ 2. Introducing CCRZ gates for controlled three-qubit interactions (more flexible than     │
│                          │ ZZZ)                                                                                      │
│                          │ 3. Keeping parameter sharing on pre/post RZ gates to maintain efficiency                  │
│                          │ 4. Adding more three-qubit interactions to capture higher-order correlations              │
│                          │ 5. Maintaining the successful CRZ two-qubit gates from the current program                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The rationale is that RX gates provide orthogonal rotations to RY, improving the          │
│                          │ expressivity of the single-qubit layer. CCRZ gates offer more controlled interactions     │
│                          │ than ZZZ, potentially better suited for the problem structure. More three-qubit           │
│                          │ interactions increase the circuit's ability to model complex relationships while          │
│                          │ parameter sharing keeps the parameter count reasonable.                                   │
