╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ split_rz_layers_asymmetric                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses a single shared "rz_pre" parameter across all 9 qubits, which is │
│                          │ highly efficient (120 total parameters) but may lack expressiveness for differentiating   │
│                          │ qubit regions. This redesign splits the pre-rotation phase layer into two asymmetric      │
│                          │ groups:                                                                                   │
│                          │ - "rz_pre_a" for qubits 0–4 (lower half, more connected in the coupling graph)            │
│                          │ - "rz_pre_b" for qubits 5–8 (upper half)                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Each group uses its own parameter, providing more phase flexibility while keeping         │
│                          │ parameter count near ~122–124. Additionally, I remove one fixed CZ gate (CZ between 1 and │
│                          │ 8) and replace it with a parametrized CRZ, adding meaningful learning capacity without    │
│                          │ bloating the parameter count. The post-rotation phase remains shared across all qubits to │
│                          │ maintain regularization. This slight structural asymmetry should better capture           │
│                          │ region-specific quantum correlations while preserving the efficiency that made the        │
│                          │ current program successful.                                                               │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0135                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5                                                     │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 0; deleted: 0; modified: 10;                                                       │
