│ patch_description        │ The first program achieved the best validation accuracy (0.62) with 186 parameters        │
│                          │ including RX gates. The current program removed RX gates and added a third ZZZ gate, both │
│                          │ of which appear to have degraded performance. This edit:                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Restores the RX layer (which was present in the best-performing variant)               │
│                          │ 2. Rewires two CRZ gates to alternative connectivity patterns: crz_2 from [0,8] to [3,6]  │
│                          │ and crz_5 from [3,5] to [4,7], following the recommendation to explore different qubit    │
│                          │ coupling maps                                                                             │
│                          │ 3. Removes the third ZZZ gate (zzz_2) that was added in the current program, as it        │
│                          │ appears to have hurt generalization                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This balances expressivity with parameter efficiency while testing new connectivity       │
│                          │ patterns that may better match the underlying data topology.                              │
