│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ parameter_sharing_zzz_expansion                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves a combined score of 0.56 with 120 parameters and reasonable  │
│                          │ validation accuracy (0.60). The prior programs show that adding three-qubit interactions  │
│                          │ (ZZZ gates) improved the score from 0.54 to 0.55. However, the current version removed    │
│                          │ the CCRZ gates to reduce parameters while keeping two ZZZ gates.                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Following the recommendation in the prompt, I propose to:                                 │
│                          │ 1. Tie together crz_0 (wires [0,2]) and crz_4 (wires [2,4]) by sharing a single parameter │
│                          │ "crz_shared_0". This saves 1 parameter slot.                                              │
│                          │ 2. Use the freed capacity to add a third ZZZ gate on wires [2,6,7] ("zzz_2").             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Rationale:                                                                                │
│                          │ - Parameter sharing has already proven effective in the current design (rz_pre and        │
│                          │ rz_post are shared across all qubits).                                                    │
│                          │ - The CRZ gates on [0,2] and [2,4] both involve qubit 2 and could benefit from correlated │
│                          │ evolution through shared parameters.                                                      │
│                          │ - Adding a third ZZZ interaction on [2,6,7] exploits a currently underutilized region of  │
│                          │ the circuit (qubits 2, 6, 7 have limited three-qubit interactions).                       │
│                          │ - This maintains the parameter count at a reasonable level while increasing expressivity  │
│                          │ through higher-order interactions.                                                        │
│                          │ - The generalization gap is already low (0.10), so adding controlled expressivity should  │
│                          │ help close the validation-test gap.                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected impact:                                                                          │
│                          │ - Validation accuracy should improve from 0.60 toward the 0.62 achieved in prior          │
│                          │ experiments.                                                                              │
│                          │ - Test accuracy should improve from 0.54 toward 0.59.                                     │
│                          │ - Parameter efficiency maintained with n_params staying low.                              │
│                          │ - Combined score should improve beyond 0.56.                                              │
