│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shared_rz_mid_layer                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current program has 186 parameters and shows signs of overfitting (train: 0.71,       │
│                          │ validation: 0.62, test: 0.59, gap: 0.12). The recommendation is to insert a shared        │
│                          │ "rz_mid" layer between the CZ/CRZ alternation and the ZZZ block. This adds minimal        │
│                          │ overhead (just 1 parameter and ~8 gates) while providing crucial phase control            │
│                          │ immediately before three-qubit interactions.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key improvements:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. Remove individual RX parameters (ry_0..ry_8, rx_0..rx_8) and replace with shared RY    │
│                          │ layer - reduces parameters from 18 to 1                                                   │
│                          │ 2. Keep the proven rz_pre shared layer                                                    │
│                          │ 3. Add a new shared rz_mid layer after CRZ/CZ gates but before ZZZ/CCRZ - provides phase  │
│                          │ flexibility before high-order interactions                                                │
│                          │ 4. Keep CCRZ gates but ensure they benefit from the rz_mid phase control                  │
│                          │ 5. Keep final rz_post shared layer                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces n_params from 186 to ~121 (9 unique params: ry_pre, rz_pre, 7×crz, zzz_0,    │
│                          │ zzz_1, ccrz_0, ccrz_1, rz_mid, rz_post), reduces depth slightly, and should improve       │
│                          │ generalization by:                                                                        │
│                          │ - Reducing parameter count (less overfitting)                                             │
│                          │ - Adding strategic phase control before three-qubit gates                                 │
│                          │ - Maintaining expressivity through CRZ and three-qubit interactions                       │
