│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ dual_zone_phase_tuning                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ This approach draws inspiration from the recommendation to split the global pre-RZ        │
│                          │ parameter into zone-specific parameters, combined with insights from the prior programs'  │
│                          │ success with parameter sharing and efficiency.                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key observations from context programs:                                                   │
│                          │ 1. Gen 1 achieved 0.58 score with 120 params and good generalization (0.09 gap)           │
│                          │ 2. Gen 2 achieved 0.59 score with only 114 params and excellent generalization (0.06 gap) │
│                          │ 3. Current program has 162 params with poor generalization (0.13 gap), suggesting         │
│                          │ overfitting                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The novel approach implements a **dual-zone phase tuning strategy**:                      │
│                          │ - Split pre-entanglement RZ into two parameters: "rz_pre_a" for qubits 0-4 (lower zone)   │
│                          │ and "rz_pre_b" for qubits 5-8 (upper zone)                                                │
│                          │ - This mirrors Gen 2's efficiency while providing finer phase control across the circuit  │
│                          │ - Reduce parameter count by removing redundant CRZ gates and consolidating three-qubit    │
│                          │ interactions                                                                              │
│                          │ - Maintain strategic two-qubit entanglement on allowed pairs only                         │
│                          │ - Use parameter sharing more aggressively to improve generalization                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This design balances expressivity with parameter efficiency, targeting the 0.06           │
│                          │ generalization gap seen in Gen 2 while maintaining validation accuracy above 0.63.        │
