│ patch_description        │ This approach uses a fundamentally different strategy focused on **selective parameter    │
│                          │ placement** and **efficient entanglement topology**. Instead of uniformly sharing         │
│                          │ parameters across all qubits or applying redundant single-qubit rotations, this design:   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Targeted encoding**: Individual RY parameters per qubit for flexible input encoding  │
│                          │ 2. **Strategic phase layer**: Shared RZ parameters for global phase coherence             │
│                          │ 3. **Optimized entanglement**: Uses a mix of parametrized (CRX, CRY, CRZ) and fixed (CZ)  │
│                          │ two-qubit gates on valid pairs, focusing on high-connectivity qubits                      │
│                          │ 4. **Three-qubit interactions**: Carefully selected ZZZ gates for enhanced expressivity   │
│                          │ without redundancy                                                                        │
│                          │ 5. **Minimal post-processing**: Single final rotation layer for output preparation        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces unnecessary gates while maintaining expressivity, targeting ~110 parameters  │
│                          │ for optimal generalization. The design emphasizes quality over quantity in both parameter │
│                          │ count and gate depth.                                                                     │
