│ patch_name               │ restore_three_qubit_expressivity_with_ccrz                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current program has degraded performance (0.56 vs 0.59 in prior best) despite having  │
│                          │ fewer parameters. The main issue is insufficient three-qubit interaction                  │
│                          │ expressivity—only 2 ZZZ gates remain.                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The strategy:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. Restore a third three-qubit gate by adding back a CCRZ on qubits [2,6,7] (as suggested │
│                          │ in the recommendation)                                                                    │
│                          │ 2. Reduce excessive parameter sharing in the single-qubit rotation layers by using        │
│                          │ distinct parameters for different qubit groups, which allows the optimizer to learn       │
│                          │ qubit-specific transformations                                                            │
│                          │ 3. This maintains parameter efficiency (~95 params) while recovering expressivity         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The CCRZ gate is lighter than ZZZ (controlled rotation vs full three-body interaction),   │
│                          │ which should help avoid overfitting while maintaining the expressivity needed for better  │
│                          │ generalization.                                                                           │
