│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ restore_individual_params_add_global_rx                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses all shared parameters (ry_pre, rz_pre, etc.) which severely      │
│                          │ limits expressivity. Prior successful programs (score 0.60) used individual parameters in │
│                          │ Layer 1 for better input encoding flexibility.                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit:                                                                                │
│                          │ 1. Restores individual RY parameters (ry_0 through ry_8) in Layer 1 instead of shared     │
│                          │ ry_pre, allowing the circuit to learn diverse input transformations per qubit             │
│                          │ 2. Inserts a shared RX global rotation layer between the initial encoding and             │
│                          │ entanglement (after rz_pre), as recommended, to diversify the basis before entanglement   │
│                          │ without adding many parameters (+1 param, +9 gates)                                       │
│                          │ 3. Keeps the efficient two-qubit and three-qubit structure                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This balances expressivity (individual input encoding) with parameter efficiency (shared  │
│                          │ global rotations), mirroring the successful strategy from prior program 2 which achieved  │
│                          │ 0.60 score with 174 params. The added global RX layer provides basis diversity similar to │
│                          │ how rz_phase worked in prior programs.                                                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
