                         Patch Metadata - Gen 41/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ restore_expressivity_strategic_sharing                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The current architecture suffers from underfitting due to excessive parameter sharing in  │
│                          │ the first layer. All ry_pre are identical, severely limiting feature extraction capacity. │
│                          │ Prior Gen 2 achieved 0.65 test accuracy with individual RY parameters plus strategic      │
│                          │ 2-qubit parametrization.                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit:                                                                                │
│                          │ 1. Restores individual RY parameters in Layer 1 (ry_0 through ry_8) to enable diverse     │
│                          │ feature encoding, matching the successful Gen 2 pattern                                   │
│                          │ 2. Merges crz_2 and crz_3 into a shared parameter "crz_mixed" on edges [0,8] and [1,3] to │
│                          │ free parameters without losing expressivity                                               │
│                          │ 3. Adds CZ gate on [3,6] to increase mid-layer connectivity on a previously weak axis     │
│                          │ 4. Removes the final redundant RZ layer (Layer 3) that contributes to depth without       │
│                          │ improving generalization                                                                  │
│                          │ 5. Keeps only one final RY layer for output preparation, reducing circuit depth           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected outcome: ~125 parameters with better expressivity, improved test accuracy to     │
│                          │ ~0.63-0.65 range, lower generalization gap, and faster convergence due to reduced depth.  │
│ num_applied              │ 3                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0198                                                                                   │
