                         Patch Metadata - Gen 44/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hierarchical_entanglement_with_adaptive_depth                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current approach uses a relatively flat, uniform ansatz with many shared parameters   │
│                          │ across all qubits. This can lead to underfitting and poor expressivity. The new approach  │
│                          │ uses a hierarchical entanglement strategy with adaptive depth:                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Sparse encoding layer**: Use RX and RY on alternating qubits to reduce parameter     │
│                          │ redundancy while maintaining expressivity.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Hierarchical entanglement**: Build entanglement in stages—first local pairs, then    │
│                          │ medium-range, then long-range—allowing the circuit to learn multi-scale correlations more │
│                          │ efficiently.                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Controlled parameter sharing**: Share parameters only within local clusters (e.g.,   │
│                          │ qubits 0-3, 4-6, 7-8) rather than globally, reducing overfitting while maintaining        │
│                          │ structure.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Reduced three-qubit gates**: Use fewer but more strategically placed three-qubit     │
│                          │ interactions (CCRZ instead of ZZZ) to boost expressivity without excessive depth.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 5. **Adaptive readout layer**: Use RX rotations at the end instead of RZ to provide       │
│                          │ orthogonal basis for measurement, potentially improving discrimination.                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach should achieve:                                                             │
│                          │ - Better generalization (lower validation-test gap)                                       │
│                          │ - Improved test accuracy through more efficient parameter use                             │
│                          │ - Faster convergence via structured entanglement                                          │
│                          │ - Lower total parameter count through strategic sharing                                   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0156                                                                                   │
