│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Costs zero parameters while improving entanglement at the output stage                 │
│                          │ 2. Captures residual correlations between qubits that are already connected via           │
│                          │ parametrized gates in Layer 3                                                             │
│                          │ 3. Mirrors the mixed-entangler strategy (parametrized + fixed gates) that proved          │
│                          │ successful in Layer 3                                                                     │
│                          │ 4. Adds only +1 depth while potentially improving expressivity                            │
│                          │ 5. Enhances information flow to the readout qubits before final preparation               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The pair (3,8) is valid per the allowed two-qubit gates list and appears in multiple      │
│                          │ parametrized interactions, making this coupling strategically positioned to capture       │
│                          │ important correlations without overfitting.                                               │
