│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ restore_ry_add_ccrz                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current program over-shares RY parameters, reducing individual qubit expressivity.    │
│                          │ Prior program 1 achieved 0.60 score with 114 parameters using individual RY gates. The    │
│                          │ recommendation suggests exploring more CCRZ gates for better expressivity.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit:                                                                                │
│                          │ 1. Restores individual RY parameters (ry_0 through ry_8) for better initial encoding      │
│                          │ 2. Replaces the ZZZ gate on [1,5,6] with a CCRZ gate to increase controlled-phase         │
│                          │ interactions                                                                              │
│                          │ 3. Adds a third CCRZ gate on [2,5,7] (replacing the second ZZZ) for enhanced multi-qubit  │
│                          │ correlations                                                                              │
│                          │ 4. Keeps shared RZ parameters (rz_pre, rz_mid, rz_post) for parameter efficiency          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach combines the expressivity gains from program 1 (individual RY gates) with   │
│                          │ the CCRZ-heavy architecture suggested in the recommendation, targeting better validation  │
│                          │ accuracy and reduced generalization gap while keeping parameter count reasonable (~115).  │
