│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_crx_cry_consolidation                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ This redesign consolidates parametrized two-qubit gates through strategic parameter       │
│                          │ sharing while introducing additional mixed-rotation entanglement. The key structural      │
│                          │ changes are:                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Parameter Consolidation**: Merge CRX gates on [0,2] and [2,4] into a single shared   │
│                          │ parameter "crx_shared", freeing one parameter slot.                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Enhanced Entanglement Diversity**: Use the freed capacity to add a CRY gate on       │
│                          │ [1,6], introducing a new entanglement edge that was previously absent. This increases the │
│                          │ expressivity of the circuit without exceeding the parameter budget.                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Streamlined Three-Qubit Layer**: Replace the CCRZ gate with an additional ZZZ gate   │
│                          │ on a different triple [1,5,6], which provides better coverage of the qubit space and may  │
│                          │ be more effective for the underlying problem structure.                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Optimized Output Layer**: Keep the final RY layer but ensure it complements the      │
│                          │ earlier rotations without redundancy.                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The motivation is that the current program (score 0.60) has good generalization (gap      │
│                          │ 0.04) but could benefit from:                                                             │
│                          │ - Better parameter efficiency (currently 0.00) by sharing similar rotations               │
│                          │ - Increased expressivity through diverse entanglement patterns (CRX/CRY/CRZ mix)          │
│                          │ - Broader qubit connectivity in the entanglement layer                                    │
│                          │ - Reduced parameter count to improve convergence and reduce overfitting risk              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach balances expressivity with efficiency, targeting validation accuracy        │
│                          │ improvement while maintaining the low generalization gap.                                 │
