│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ restore_individual_ry_reduce_rz_add_cnot                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current program suffers from over-aggressive parameter sharing in Layer 1, where all  │
│                          │ 9 RY gates share a single parameter "ry_pre" and all 9 RZ gates share "rz_pre". This      │
│                          │ severely limits the model's ability to learn diverse input encodings. Prior successful    │
│                          │ programs (score 0.60) used individual RY parameters per qubit, achieving better accuracy. │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Additionally, the circuit has three separate shared RZ layers (pre, mid, post), which is  │
│                          │ redundant. The current design trades expressivity for parameter efficiency but ends up    │
│                          │ with worse performance.                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit:                                                                                │
│                          │ 1. Restores individual RY parameters for each qubit (like prior programs) to improve      │
│                          │ input encoding expressivity                                                               │
│                          │ 2. Removes the redundant "rz_mid" layer to reduce circuit depth and gate count            │
│                          │ 3. Replaces the CZ gate at [2,6] with CNOT as suggested in the recommendation to test     │
│                          │ asymmetric two-qubit coupling                                                             │
│                          │ 4. Keeps the three-qubit interactions (ZZZ and CCRZ) which provide expressivity           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should improve validation accuracy and reduce the train-test gap while maintaining   │
│                          │ reasonable parameter efficiency.                                                          │
│ num_applied              │ 3                                                                                         │
