╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ asymmetric_entanglement_compact                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ This program combines insights from the best-performing variant (program 2, which         │
│                          │ achieved 0.65 test accuracy) with the recommendation to use CNOT for asymmetric coupling. │
│                          │ The key improvements are:                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Simplified structure**: Removes the excessive pre-entanglement layers (RZ + RX       │
│                          │ global) that added 27 gates without improving performance                                 │
│                          │ 2. **Asymmetric coupling**: Replaces CZ(2,6) with CNOT(2,6) to test whether directed      │
│                          │ information flow improves expressivity                                                    │
│                          │ 3. **Efficient parameter sharing**: Uses shared parameters strategically (rz_phase for    │
│                          │ all RZ gates in Layer 2)                                                                  │
│                          │ 4. **Reduced depth**: Consolidates to 5 main layers instead of scattered operations,      │
│                          │ reducing depth from 81 to ~55                                                             │
│                          │ 5. **Better generalization**: Fewer total gates (≈250 vs 393) while maintaining           │
│                          │ expressivity through three-qubit interactions                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The circuit structure:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Layer 1: Individual RY encoding (9 params)                                              │
│                          │ - Layer 2: Shared RZ phase (1 param)                                                      │
│                          │ - Layer 3: Mixed entanglement with CRX/CRY/CRZ and one CNOT (asymmetric) (7 params)       │
│                          │ - Layer 4: Three-qubit interactions (ZZZ + CCRZ) (3 params)                               │
│                          │ - Layer 5: Final RY output preparation (9 params)                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Total: ~29 parameters, significantly more efficient than current 144, while maintaining   │
│                          │ the expressivity that made program 2 successful.                                          │
