                         Patch Metadata - Gen 54/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ asymmetric_cnot_enhanced_expressivity                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The current program (score 0.60) shows a large generalization gap (0.09) and lower test   │
│                          │ accuracy (0.58) despite decent validation accuracy (0.65). Key issues:                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Generalization gap too large**: The gap between validation (0.65) and test (0.58)    │
│                          │ suggests overfitting. The current architecture uses heavy parameter sharing which may     │
│                          │ limit model capacity.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Parameter efficiency underutilized**: With only 114 parameters, the model is too     │
│                          │ constrained. Previous program 2 used 174 parameters and achieved better test accuracy     │
│                          │ (0.65).                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Fixed CZ gates may be insufficient**: The all-CZ two-qubit layer provides symmetric  │
│                          │ coupling, which may not capture asymmetric correlations in the data.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **New strategy:**                                                                         │
│                          │ - Replace some fixed CZ gates with CNOT gates to introduce asymmetric two-qubit           │
│                          │ interactions that can model directional information flow                                  │
│                          │ - Reduce parameter sharing in the entanglement layer to increase expressivity and model   │
│                          │ capacity                                                                                  │
│                          │ - Add dedicated parameters to more CRZ gates instead of sharing them broadly              │
│                          │ - Maintain three-qubit interactions but add another CCRZ for richer interactions          │
│                          │ - Keep shared single-qubit rotations for efficiency but give entanglement layers more     │
│                          │ freedom                                                                                   │
