│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ symmetric_param_sharing_reduce_overfit                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The current program suffers from severe overfitting (77% train vs 65% validation,         │
│                          │ generalization gap 0.13) with 222 parameters. The second program achieved better          │
│                          │ performance (score 0.61) with 174 parameters by using shared parameters like `rz_phase`.  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit implements symmetric parameter sharing:                                         │
│                          │ 1. Replace individual final RZ parameters (rz_0 through rz_8) with a shared `rz_final`    │
│                          │ parameter                                                                                 │
│                          │ 2. Share CRX parameters symmetrically: crx_0 and crx_1 → crx_shared, crx_2 stays unique   │
│                          │ 3. Share CRY parameters symmetrically: cry_0 and cry_1 → cry_shared                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces parameters from 222 to ~195 while maintaining expressivity through the       │
│                          │ proven pattern of selective sharing. The goal is to reduce overfitting and improve the    │
│                          │ generalization gap, similar to how the second program achieved its better performance.    │
