│ patch_description        │ The second program achieved better performance (0.61 vs 0.60) with validation accuracy of │
│                          │ 0.68 by using RY gates for output preparation instead of RZ. Additionally, the            │
│                          │ recommendation suggests adding a lightweight non-parametric CZ sublayer to reinforce      │
│                          │ connectivity.                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit:                                                                                │
│                          │ 1. Inserts three fixed CZ gates on non-adjacent allowed pairs (2,7), (3,6), (4,5) before  │
│                          │ the final output layer to improve entanglement without adding parameters                  │
│                          │ 2. Replaces the final RZ layer with RY gates for better output preparation (matching the  │
│                          │ better-performing second program)                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This leverages the low-gap benefits of fixed two-qubit couplings at minimal depth and     │
│                          │ gate-count cost, while improving output expressivity through RY rotations.                │
