                         Patch Metadata - Gen 73/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ restore_and_phase_enhance                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current program has regressed to a score of 0.57 from Program 2's better score of     │
│                          │ 0.61. The main issues are:                                                                │
│                          │ 1. Extra RX global layer adds unnecessary depth without proportional benefit              │
│                          │ 2. Excessive intermediate RZ layers (rz_mid) increase complexity                          │
│                          │ 3. Too many three-qubit gates (2 ZZZ + 2 CCRZ) creates overparameterization               │
│                          │ 4. Overall depth (81) and gate count (393) are too high                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The solution: Return to Program 2's proven successful structure (which had individual RY, │
│                          │ shared RZ phase, mixed parametrized 2-qubit gates, and final RY output) and add a second  │
│                          │ shared RZ phase layer immediately after the three-qubit block. This follows the           │
│                          │ recommendation to capture deeper phase correlations at minimal cost (1 parameter).        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected improvements:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Reduce depth and gate count closer to Program 2 levels                                  │
│                          │ - Restore the good train/val accuracy balance from Program 2                              │
