│                          │ qubits, which provide crucial output preparation and improve generalization.              │
│                          │ Additionally, the recommendation suggests adding a second shared RZ phase layer to probe  │
│                          │ deeper global coherence effects.                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit restores the final RY layer (which was in the high-performing Program 2) and    │
│                          │ adds a second shared RZ phase layer (rz_phase2) after the three-qubit interactions. This  │
│                          │ combination:                                                                              │
│                          │ 1. Restores output preparation capability that improved validation accuracy in Program 2  │
│                          │ 2. Adds deeper global phase control for enhanced expressivity                             │
│                          │ 3. Maintains parameter efficiency by using shared parameters                              │
│                          │ 4. Should reduce the train-test gap by improving output encoding                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The pattern of shared RZ layers bookending the entanglement blocks has proven effective   │
│                          │ in prior iterations.                                                                      │
