│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ tie_symmetric_entanglement_params                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The current circuit has 174 parameters, which is significantly over-parameterized         │
│                          │ compared to the prior 114-parameter version that achieved nearly the same score (0.60 vs  │
│                          │ 0.61). The recommendation suggests tying symmetric two-qubit rotation parameters in the   │
│                          │ mixed entanglement layer.                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Specifically:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. Merge crz_0 & crz_3 into "crz_s1" (both control-target pairs on non-adjacent qubits)   │
│                          │ 2. Merge crz_2 & crz_6 into "crz_s2" (similar symmetric pattern)                          │
│                          │ 3. Merge cry_1 & cry_5 into "cry_s" (symmetric CRY gates)                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Additionally, the output layer has 9 individual RY parameters that can be shared in an    │
│                          │ alternating pattern (similar to the input layer's proven ry_0/ry_1 pattern), reducing     │
│                          │ from 9 to 2 parameters.                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces the parameter count from 174 to approximately 156, improving parameter       │
│                          │ efficiency while preserving the circuit's expressivity through the proven entanglement    │
│                          │ structure. The symmetric sharing follows the success of global RZ sharing and respects    │
│                          │ the nonadjacent connectivity constraints.                                                 │
