│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ consolidated_zzz_reduced_params                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current program (score 0.58) has degraded compared to the second prior program (score │
│                          │ 0.61). Analysis shows:                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Parameter bloat**: Current has 186 params vs. 174 in the best prior. The mirror ZZZ  │
│                          │ block with shared "zzz_mirror" parameter adds redundancy without clear benefit.           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Generalization gap**: Current gap is 0.10 vs. 0.07 in the best prior, indicating     │
│                          │ overfitting.                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Gate count explosion**: 351 gates vs. 279 in the best prior suggests unnecessary     │
│                          │ depth.                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Strategy**: Consolidate back to the structure of the best prior (score 0.61) but with   │
│                          │ targeted improvements:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Remove the redundant mirror ZZZ block that inflates parameters and depth                │
│                          │ - Consolidate the two ZZZ interactions [0,4,8] and [2,5,7] under a single shared          │
│                          │ parameter "zzz_shared" to reduce parameter count while maintaining expressivity           │
│                          │ - Keep the proven two-qubit entanglement structure from the best prior                    │
│                          │ - Reduce the mid-layer RZ to only apply to critical qubits instead of all 9               │
│                          │ - Use parameter efficiency more strategically                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This targets:                                                                             │
│                          │ - Lower parameter count (target ~140-150 params)                                          │
│                          │ - Reduced generalization gap (back toward 0.07)                                           │
│                          │ - Improved validation accuracy (maintain ~0.68)                                           │
│                          │ - Better parameter efficiency without sacrificing expressivity                            │
